          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="b977-7c5e-33b2-428e"/>
            <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="fd7f-888d-3257-a12b">This unit cannot have grudge marks and cannot be affected by **^^Ancestral Vow^^** abilities.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Too Stubborn to Die" id="9495-7a6c-bd13-3c1d" hidden="false" typeId="907f-a48-6a04-f788" typeName="Ability (Passive)">
          <attributes>
            <attribute name="Color" typeId="50fe-4f29-6bc3-dcc6">Yellow</attribute>
            <attribute name="Type" typeId="bf11-4e10-3ab1-06f4">Rallying</attribute>
            <attribute name="Parent Node" typeId="e2e1-15ca-d345-22b8"/>
          </attributes>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="b977-7c5e-33b2-428e"/>
            <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="fd7f-888d-3257-a12b">The first time this unit would be destroyed, before removing it from play, roll a dice. On a 3+, this unit is not destroyed and any remaining damage points inflicted on it have no effect. Then, Heal (D3) this unit.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="A Glorious Doom" id="ec75-89b8-4e9b-beed" hidden="false" typeId="907f-a48-6a04-f788" typeName="Ability (Passive)">
          <attributes>
            <attribute name="Color" typeId="50fe-4f29-6bc3-dcc6">Red</attribute>
            <attribute name="Type" typeId="bf11-4e10-3ab1-06f4">Offensive</attribute>
            <attribute name="Parent Node" typeId="e2e1-15ca-d345-22b8"/>
          </attributes>
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Keywords" typeId="b977-7c5e-33b2-428e"/>
            <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="fd7f-888d-3257-a12b">While this unit is in combat with any enemy **^^Heroes^^** or **^^Monsters^^**:
• It can only pick those enemy units to be the targets of its combat attacks.
• Add 2 to the Attacks characteristic of this unit&apos;s melee weapons for each enemy **^^Hero^^** or **^^Monster^^** unit in combat with it.
**Designer&apos;s Note:** *A unit with both the **^^Hero^^** and **^^Monster^^** keywords only adds 2 to the Attacks characteristic of this unit&apos;s melee weapons.*</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
